2026-09-26T08:57:21.8233739Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8233960Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234041Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234143Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234226Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234324Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234403Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234508Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234587Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8234681Z             return x + 1
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8242448Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8242560Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8242676Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8242780Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8242856Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8242937Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243046Z     To execute it::
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243121Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243208Z         $ pytest
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243390Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243487Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243569Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243667Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243747Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8243899Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244080Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244161Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244255Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244354Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244448Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244545Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244619Z     
2026-09-26T08:57:21.8244734Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
